From 83d17d2273627adf1cfe1b5826584c1d069b1cc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:09:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a held tui claim the wake settled stays
 resolved after recovery; the legacy poller sees gateway ownership on the
 lineage root and its turn lease

Review rework for PR #1720 (t_01a1cfbe6c8d46e7):

- Review 5881204008 (t_01a1d154902ba0a7): settle_held fell back to the buffer's own
  start when recovery had already cleared a claim the wake settled through its end, so an
  archived card's delivered completion stayed buffered for a second turn. With no claim in
  flight the row's cursor is the settlement evidence; a resolved claim with nothing left in
  flight is dropped instead of lingering as an empty durable claim.
- Review 5881224107 (t_01a1d1543b9d13cf): gateway_owns checked the ledger only for the tui
  tip. It now checks the chat and its compaction parents, like _gateway_holds_work, and also
  hands back while the live gateway's pid holds the chat's turn lease.
- local_since's created_at fallback counts a same-second event as before the row (the tui
  leg keeps it: a duplicate beats a lost notice).
